  "operative_text": "Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.110): No dealer may deliver firearms or ammunition in excess of the limits established in section 2 of this act.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 2 (new section, chapter 9.41 RCW): (1)(a) A dealer may not deliver more than one firearm to a purchaser or transferee within any 30-day period.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 2 (new section, chapter 9.41 RCW): (b) A dealer may not deliver more than 100 rounds of .50 caliber ammunition or more than 1,000 rounds of any other caliber of ammunition to a purchaser or transferee within any 30-day period.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 2 (new section, chapter 9.41 RCW): (3) Compliance with this section is a condition of dealer licensure under RCW 9.41.110. A violation of this section is punishable by forfeiture of the dealer's license."
